  title: Hoysalas
  text: The Hoysalas ruled southern Karnataka from the 11th to the 14th centuries, from Dvarasamudra, now Halebidu. Their star-shaped temples at Belur, Halebidu and Somanathapura, richly carved in soapstone, are UNESCO World Heritage Sites.
